  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04HR">Lemma <span data-tag="04HR">34.4.12</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathit{Sch}_{\acute{e}tale}$ be a big étale site containing $S$. The functor $S_{affine, {\acute{e}tale}} \to S_{\acute{e}tale}$ is special cocontinuous and induces an equivalence of topoi from $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (S_{affine, {\acute{e}tale}})$ to $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (S_{\acute{e}tale})$. </p>
